  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **These Memories of You**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **Fiddlers Dream**: back after 95 archived shows (379 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Little Cabin Home on the Hill**: rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **Last Day at Gettysburg**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **The Preacher and the Bear**: rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **Windy and Warm**: rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Oh Where is My Boy Tonight**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Big Sandy River**: rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **familystrings2020-02-29.litz.schoepsMK21.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 27 songs; 114 min [1]\n- **billystrings2020-02-29.MG20**: source not stated; 28 songs; 115 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Microphones were placed on stage, in front of the right-side PA [1]\n- Microphones were positioned about one foot from an onstage monitor fill [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **familystrings2020-02-29.litz.schoepsMK21.flac16**: taped by Keith Litzenberger; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps MK21's(On Stage,in front of right side PA)>Schoeps KCY 250/051>Schoeps VST62iu>Sound Devices MixPre-10 II (Recorded at 32 Bit Float/44.1 Khz) [1]. Also: Chain continues to a Sound Devices MixPre-10 II at 32-bit float, then Sound Forge Pro 13 for fades and 16-bit conversion, then FLAC [1]\n- **billystrings2020-02-29.MG20**: taped by Keith Antaya; transferred by Keith Antaya; source: MG20>nBob actives>Sound Devices MP10ii [2]. Also: Recorded with MG20 microphones through nBob active adapters into a Sound Devices MixPre 10ii at 32-bit float; Transfer from SDHC card through Adobe Audition 3.0 and CDWave 1.71 [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by thecurtainwithblog.blogspot.com: [Billy Strings - 2020-02-29 Ionia Theatre, Ionia, MI](https://thecurtainwithblog.blogspot.com/2020/03/billy-strings-2020-02-29-ionia-theatre.html) [4]",
